Jenny: Hi Beth, love, ok? Beth: Yeah, bit shattered, kaafi kaam kar rahi hu aajkal. Jenny: Well, mere khyaal se ye tera sabse zyada busy time hai! Beth: Yeah, but mujhe nahi acha lag raha! Humara abhi presale weekend aaya tha, aadhi raat tak kaam karna pada. Fir sale week, ab Christmas and and mai Christmas Eve pe late tak kaam kar rahi hu, fir subah 6 am start karna hai Boxing Day pe and 8am New Year's Day pe. Jenny: Wow! Yaha toh kaafi slave drivers hai! Samuel's mei toh itna kuch bura nahi hai, bas thode se busy din aur ek late night till 8pm.Mai toh yaha kaafi enjoy karti hu, actually. Beth: Mai toh regret karna shuru kar rahi ye job, wo extra hours pile karte rehte hai short notice pe and tum inhe sirf 3 hafte pehle hi change kara sakte ho. Plus, busy periods mei wese bhi chhuti nahi le sakte. Jenny: Toh basically tumhari koi chhuti nahi hui iss saal? Beth: Nope, bilkul nahi! Christmas Day, shayad se, but fir mujhe agle din Stupid o' Clock pe uthna hai Boxing Day pe! Jenny: So, no good suggesting a drink one night? Beth: Mai 27th tak free hu kyuki mujhe 28th ko 2pm tak nahi jaana. But uske baad 7 ghante ki shift hai, toh kisi type ka hangover nahi le sakti! Jenny: Hai bhagwan, it does suck a bit, but atleast tum decent toh kama rahi ho. Beth: Yes, I suppose so and humare paas profits share scheme bhi hai toh bonus bhi milta hai. But koi work/life balance nahi hai.😢 Jenny: Do you think you'll get taken on in the New Year?God Beth: Umm, pata nahi. Maine ek din bhi miss nahi kiya hai, 5 minute late hone ke liye paycut liya hai! Mai frankly sure nahi hu ki mai job chahti bhi hu ya nahi, mind you. Jenny: Yes, mai pros aur cons ke baare mei bohot carefully sochungi! Beth: Yes, mai dekhungi aaspaas, check Indeed, Reed, etc, other job sites. Jenny: Mai bhi apne kaan khule rakhungi, dekhti hu shehar mei kya hai aaspaas, ek doosre ke aaspaas kaam karne mei acha lagega! Beth: Yes, it would! Thanks love, coffee ke liye milte hai ek din toh. Jenny: OK, tell me when you're off next and hum hopefully kuch na kuch sort kar lenge. Beth: OK, sounds good, Bye!
