Sam: Mai recent events se kaafi baffled hu Pam: Kya matlab tumhara, Sammo? Sam: Mai iss populism and sharpened language ki wave jo politicians use karte hai unse kaafi distressed hu. Wo sirf immigration, stigmatised and attacked groups ke subjects ke neeche aag lagate hai, real problems pe nahi. Kisi ko economy aur human rights se farak nahi padta Pam: Yeah, mere hisaab se aajkal kaafi log unconsious hai media ke tabloidisation ki wajeh se. Hum esi short themed news padte hai jo itne ache se prepared hoti hai ki wo logo mei strong emotions generate karti hai. Sam: Hm, mujhe iska koi solution dikh toh nahi raha. I am afraid, that the fake news industry is only set to gain meaning aaj ke internet pe.Prosecute karna bohot mushkil hoga aajkal ke falsehood pe, jisse pehle ki it gets bigger meaning and recognition. Pam: Yes, impossible toh hai. Aajkal kam se kam log bade forms padhte hai, such as books, reports or reportages. Sab kuch black or white, ab political debates well driven facts ke saath toh hoti hi nahi hai. Ab sirf insults, made up numbers aur stats se opinion prove hota hai. Sam: I could not have said it better… 
